# BLOCK 2B: template for /home/wizard-deploy/nflprops/nflprops-runtime.env
# on the Wizard host (the probe found wizard-deploy cannot write /etc, so
# the env file lives inside the isolated nflprops root). deploy-wizard.yml
# copies this template there ONLY if absent (never overwriting real
# values) with mode 600; to do it by hand, as wizard-deploy:
#
#   install -m 600 deploy/systemd/nflprops-runtime.env.example \
#     /home/wizard-deploy/nflprops/nflprops-runtime.env
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in file -- it is deliberately outside git
# (deploy/systemd/*.env is gitignored; only this *.env.example template is
# tracked). Referenced by deploy/systemd/nflprops-runtime.service via
# EnvironmentFile=.

# The locked zero-cost architecture (docs/PLATFORM_AUTOMATION.md, BLOCK 2B):
# DuckDB + versioned immutable snapshots is production truth here, no
# database server required. NFLPROPS_DATA_ROOT MUST be an explicit absolute
# path in production (nflprops.data.storage.settings.StorageSettings
# enforces this).
NFLPROPS_ENV=production
NFLPROPS_STORAGE_BACKEND=duckdb
NFLPROPS_DATA_ROOT=/home/wizard-deploy/nflprops/state/warehouse

# The probe-approved isolated runtime root: snapshots/, publications/,
# backups/, logs/, locks/ live directly under it
# (nflprops.platform.runtime_layout).
NFLPROPS_RUNTIME_ROOT=/home/wizard-deploy/nflprops

# Bounded snapshot retention (~11 GB free at probe time) -- never unlimited.
NFLPROPS_SNAPSHOT_RETENTION=7

# The running release's git SHA is read from <release>/RELEASE_SHA (written
# by deploy/wizard/prepare_release.sh). Do NOT set
# NFLPROPS_RUNTIME_VERSION_SHA here: it would override that marker for
# every release and make the deploy gate's --expect-version check fail.

# Optional: logging level.
NFLPROPS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Future API (not deployed in BLOCK 2B): localhost-only, single worker.
# Pick the port at deployment time after re-checking `ss -tln` -- never
# 8000 or 8080 (occupied; nflprops.platform.runtime_layout.validate_api_port).
# NFLPROPS_API_PORT=

# Provider API key(s), only if/when continuous collection is activated
# (Block 3) -- never populated by BLOCK 2B itself.
BDL_API_KEY=
